{
  "id": "semantic_tokens/lexical/13_doc_comments",
  "topic": "semantic_tokens",
  "subtopic": "lexical",
  "title": "Documentation comments",
  "summary": "Commands in documentation comments are keywords, the names they document parameters",
  "prose": "Inside a `///` or `/** */` comment, a command such as `\\param`, `@brief`\nor `@return` is a `keyword` and the name after `@param` a `parameter`,\nboth with the `documentation` modifier; the rest of the comment stays a\n`comment`. An ordinary comment has no commands.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "/// Scales a value.\n/// \\param value the value to scale\n/// @param factor how much, at least 1\n/// @return the scaled value\nint scale(int value, int factor);\n\n/**\n * @brief A point on the plane.\n * @tparam T the coordinate type\n */\ntemplate <class T>\nstruct Point {\n    T x, y;\n};\n\n///@brief Clamps a value.\nint clamp(int value);\n\n// @param plain comments have no commands\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
